                    {
                        "form_id": "d4a62ae2-ba09-47b4-9759-64170ce09f3f",
                        "entry_id": "1ed9c79a-759b-3114-ba3e-44276d43a7a4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "мириа́дах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ef453b06-3942-3f82-b56c-44fd2feddd58",
                        "entry_id": "1ed9c79a-759b-3114-ba3e-44276d43a7a4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. десять тысяч; число, равное 10⁴"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6964b9c2-e3cb-4791-92df-6d329e5151ba",
                                "sense_id": "ef453b06-3942-3f82-b56c-44fd2feddd58",
                                "text": "До Архимеда в Древней Греции самым большим числом считалось 10 000 000, т.е. 1000 мириад (мириадой называлось число 10 000 от греческого слова «мириос» — «неисчислимо большое»)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5f3930b-9724-4170-a099-3da1c067410e",
                                "sense_id": "ef453b06-3942-3f82-b56c-44fd2feddd58",
                                "text": "Всего в данном отрывке Ипполит приводит 13 чисел, относящихся к расстояниям между небесными телами. Расстояния исчисляются тысячами мириад стадий и даны с точностью до стадии."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e8a806c1-8119-30a2-8e6e-e1effd943818",
                        "entry_id": "1ed9c79a-759b-3114-ba3e-44276d43a7a4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "мн. ч., поэт. бесчисленное количество, неисчислимое множество"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "53e716ca-7f8f-498e-a292-673c389eecba",
                                "sense_id": "e8a806c1-8119-30a2-8e6e-e1effd943818",
                                "text": "Ночь ложилась над городом, и вся необъятная, вспухшая от замёрзшего снега поляна Невы, с последним отблеском солнца, осыпалась бесконечными мириадами искр иглистого инея."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bf6c4ffa-5159-4ba9-a443-3227a639f86b",
                                "sense_id": "e8a806c1-8119-30a2-8e6e-e1effd943818",
                                "text": "Да сыплет ночь своей бездонной урной // К нам мириады звёзд."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "beca4b91-eb32-4e75-aacb-e84f8bcb2367",
                                "sense_id": "e8a806c1-8119-30a2-8e6e-e1effd943818",
                                "text": "В капителях колонн, когда погасало электричество, загорались мириады светляков, а в воздухе плыли болотные огни."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "08833d61-6363-4d37-9799-876fc58ee3cc",
                        "source_entry_id": "1ed9c79a-759b-3114-ba3e-44276d43a7a4",
                        "source_sense_description": "число",
                        "target_lang_word": "myriad",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "myriad",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "edf1a101-7a9d-35c9-8fe6-24946f24c1eb",
                                        "entry_id": "cf7bae7b-9f98-313d-8e33-8205e6903e70",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ten thousand; 10,000"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "52773576-12db-3fb2-8ea9-fe63e2306875",
                                        "entry_id": "cf7bae7b-9f98-313d-8e33-8205e6903e70",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ten thousand; 10,000",
                                            "Synonym of decamillennium: a period of 10000 years."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "25f760fc-aca4-3482-959a-bd9e2228e6af",
                                        "entry_id": "cf7bae7b-9f98-313d-8e33-8205e6903e70",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A countless number or multitude (of specified things)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01340b4c-47de-472d-af71-1a1849875076",
                                                "sense_id": "25f760fc-aca4-3482-959a-bd9e2228e6af",
                                                "text": "Earth hosts a myriad of animals."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e90f0ef-dd13-4277-97ab-9dd7ace7c8bc",
                                                "sense_id": "25f760fc-aca4-3482-959a-bd9e2228e6af",
                                                "text": "O Myriads of immortal Spirits, O Powers / Matchleſs, but with th' Almighty, and that ſtrife / Was not inglorious, though th' event was dire,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3fc4b28d-ded2-4e54-93b8-f095350ace0b",
                                                "sense_id": "25f760fc-aca4-3482-959a-bd9e2228e6af",
                                                "text": "A myriad of beginnings to her intended discourse darted into her mind; but, as is usual in such cases, she chose the one the very worst suited to her purpose. \"I never intend to marry,\" said she, in a faltering voice."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f86e9f9e-b186-4401-949f-da287fa0ac21",
                                                "sense_id": "25f760fc-aca4-3482-959a-bd9e2228e6af",
                                                "text": "I saw battle-corpses, myriads of them, / And the white skeletons of young men, I saw them, / I saw the debris and debris of all the slain soldiers of the war, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ebd1e08-74fa-4e7e-86e8-fecda4ca7a8f",
                                                "sense_id": "25f760fc-aca4-3482-959a-bd9e2228e6af",
                                                "text": "How far he surpassed them all may be felt if we remember that no Scythian, although the Scythians are reckoned by their myriads, has ever succeeded in dominating a foreign nation ..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "myriad",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "da99532f-9dfe-350b-b1e7-2fee7b651398",
                                        "entry_id": "ee570459-9e3c-305c-a2ab-0810a038ff18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Multifaceted, having innumerable elements"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "355a81d3-1aba-4e25-a2e4-f1eb496c64cf",
                                                "sense_id": "da99532f-9dfe-350b-b1e7-2fee7b651398",
                                                "text": "one night he would be singing at the barred window and yelling down out of the soft myriad darkness of a May night; the next night he would be gone [...]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d670947b-3fa9-4285-8fee-e73a9441f12d",
                                                "sense_id": "da99532f-9dfe-350b-b1e7-2fee7b651398",
                                                "text": "\"As a clinician, it's a difficult symptom to treat,\" Cornelius said. \"The end symptom may be the same, but what's causing it may be myriad.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "10f5c14f-cf76-378c-8765-371f8fe46250",
                                        "entry_id": "ee570459-9e3c-305c-a2ab-0810a038ff18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Great in number; innumerable, multitudinous"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c894dfc3-a344-4415-b95c-119208a49e2f",
                                                "sense_id": "10f5c14f-cf76-378c-8765-371f8fe46250",
                                                "text": "Driven by a perceived political need to adopt a hard-line stance, Mr. Cameron’s coalition government has imposed myriad new restrictions, the aim of which is to reduce net migration to Britain to below 100,000."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ee14992-1a7a-4054-96b5-56f72dc7dc12",
                                                "sense_id": "10f5c14f-cf76-378c-8765-371f8fe46250",
                                                "text": "Earth hosts myriad animals."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ebc60fa2-e2ca-4e61-8937-c4396c97c349",
                        "source_entry_id": "1ed9c79a-759b-3114-ba3e-44276d43a7a4",
                        "source_sense_description": "число",
                        "target_lang_word": "Myriade",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Myriade",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2f714cf6-9b10-32ff-8d14-b6d535746924",
                                        "entry_id": "6cc8a2c3-c6e3-385c-8cc7-938e74d85709",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "zehntausend"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d28c8ba8-8a29-456a-9f78-84ae5247aa92",
                                                "sense_id": "2f714cf6-9b10-32ff-8d14-b6d535746924",
                                                "text": "Eine Myriade entsprach bei den alten Griechen dem Wert 10.000, hundert Myriaden waren also eine Million."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6cd6c087-afeb-35d3-b5b5-ef385a30e068",
                                        "entry_id": "6cc8a2c3-c6e3-385c-8cc7-938e74d85709",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "eine sehr große, aber unbestimmte Zahl"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural-normally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd62e30e-c03c-4cbe-b57f-70769b319241",
                                                "sense_id": "6cd6c087-afeb-35d3-b5b5-ef385a30e068",
                                                "text": "Nachdem die Presse vom bevorstehenden astronomischen Ereignis berichtet hatte, stand morgens um drei eine Myriade von schlaftrunkenen Neugierigen auf dem Schlossplatz und schaute auf zu den Myriaden von Sternen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbf34660-f3ac-4400-adfd-0b30b20c60da",
                                                "sense_id": "6cd6c087-afeb-35d3-b5b5-ef385a30e068",
                                                "text": "„Wir hatten gemeinsam geduscht und schauderten beim Anblick der Myriaden von Silberfischchen, die das Badezimmer bevölkerten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8f61b41-f8e4-4ac1-b635-624fbe498623",
                                                "sense_id": "6cd6c087-afeb-35d3-b5b5-ef385a30e068",
                                                "text": "„Die aus Myriaden von Einzelheiten bestehende Vergangenheit geht in uns ein und verschwindet.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97e3047a-4178-4c18-9c42-5188c884fc13",
                                                "sense_id": "6cd6c087-afeb-35d3-b5b5-ef385a30e068",
                                                "text": "„Sie wurde sich der Myriaden von Leben in sich bewußt.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "abaca604-bcb1-4ac0-8edb-b0db2d9de016",
                        "source_entry_id": "1ed9c79a-759b-3114-ba3e-44276d43a7a4",
                        "source_sense_description": "число",
                        "target_lang_word": "myriade",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "myriade",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4d389b86-a95e-3c46-b520-f4abfc14a50f",
                                        "entry_id": "bab4a58e-0629-313a-abc4-318c621a50bf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dix-mille."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ancient"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c0103bb-5732-3a8a-8aae-36dc18701a88",
                                        "entry_id": "bab4a58e-0629-313a-abc4-318c621a50bf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Quantité indéfinie et innombrable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "collective"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bf50e13-690e-4d0b-a946-ccdfa6d3eadf",
                                                "sense_id": "2c0103bb-5732-3a8a-8aae-36dc18701a88",
                                                "text": "Mais baissez-vous, regardez à vos pieds, et partout la vie éclatera pour ainsi dire à vos regards en myriades d’êtres aux formes bizarres, à la nature ambiguë."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e19dd5c5-7e13-45be-816d-c41b43fc6660",
                                                "sense_id": "2c0103bb-5732-3a8a-8aae-36dc18701a88",
                                                "text": "[…] mais les citernes sont taries et le fond n’est plus qu’une croûte noire et vaseuse dans laquelle une myriade d’animaux immondes prennent leurs ébats […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be8e9509-1519-4925-b744-342d4a47acef",
                                                "sense_id": "2c0103bb-5732-3a8a-8aae-36dc18701a88",
                                                "text": "Ces îlots, constitués de basalte, servent de repaires à des myriades d’eiders qui nichent dans les rochers. Ces oiseaux donnent le précieux duvet connu sous le nom d’édredon, et sont la principale ressource des habitants : la loi défend de les tuer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66efd534-71c8-445f-8d15-10dd41018be8",
                                                "sense_id": "2c0103bb-5732-3a8a-8aae-36dc18701a88",
                                                "text": "Cette transformation générale de la société ne se fera pas par la prise du pouvoir d'État par une majorité de gauche ; elle suppose une myriade de luttes locales et globales."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e80e2f4-9874-42cf-9b17-675b39784616",
                                                "sense_id": "2c0103bb-5732-3a8a-8aae-36dc18701a88",
                                                "text": "Le confinement de sa propre pensée à l’égard de l’en­viron­ne­ment sus-jacent, de sa bulle ambiante, permet de mieux ré­fléchir, de commu­niquer sub­li­mi­­na­lement avec l’extérieur, de ratiociner la my­ria­­de d’observations organolep­tiques acquises, de les distiller dans les cornues du laboratoire mental de la créativité et, enfin, de les faire fondre dans les creusets intellectuels mi­niaturés des haïkus."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90bfd97c-350d-47d1-b1c1-54737710ac5d",
                                                "sense_id": "2c0103bb-5732-3a8a-8aae-36dc18701a88",
                                                "text": "Ici comme là-bas, des myriades d’oiseaux animaient cette partie du continent polaire."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
